From: Ferestre contributors
Subject: Harden game saves, message dialogs and the PlayFab save bridge

A headless message dialog is dismissed, so it completes with the title's
cancel button rather than the focused default, which is often the
destructive answer ("delete this save?").

The package identity and the MicrosoftGame.config cache are resolved under
InitOnce, so concurrent first callers no longer see "done" before the family
name exists and send saves to Packages\UnknownPackage.

A container manifest that exists but cannot be read is an error, as an
unreadable index already is; only a missing one is an empty container. An
update no longer rebuilds an unreadable container from its own blobs alone.

When several <XUID>_<SCID> folders exist, the configured user's (XGR_XUID)
is used, otherwise the one whose index was written last, ties going to the
lowest name, with a warning; never whichever the listing returned first.

XGameSaveSubmitUpdateAsync and XGameSaveDeleteContainerAsync do their disk
work on a background writer, in submission order, instead of on the caller's
thread. Container and update handles are reference counted so a title may
close them while the work is pending.

The PFX bridge clears a reused XAsyncBlock before starting the SDK operation,
returns the folder path itself as the async payload, and only treats a
payload it produced as a folder result. The cached backend DLL is copied
under a temporary name and renamed into place, reused only at the source's
size, and copied again once if it does not load. The temporary
ForceUseInprocGameSaves override is recorded in a marker first, and a run
that finds the marker restores the prior setting if the override is still in
place.

